<div class="rbmgr-wrap">
  <section class="rbmgr-intro">
    <p class="rbmgr-eyebrow">Google Reviews</p>
    <h2 class="rbmgr-heading">What Families Say</h2>

    <div class="rbmgr-rating-row" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars from 7 Google reviews">
      <span class="rbmgr-rating-number">5.0</span>
      <span class="rbmgr-stars" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
      <span class="rbmgr-review-count">7 Google reviews</span>
    </div>

    <p class="rbmgr-intro-copy">
      Music lessons are personal. Here&#8217;s what students and families have said
      about their experience at Amherst Red Barn Music School.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="rbmgr-grid" aria-label="Selected Google reviews">

    <article class="rbmgr-card rbmgr-featured">
      <h3 class="rbmgr-reviewer">Ginny Hamilton</h3>
      <div class="rbmgr-card-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-short-text">
        &#8220;Love this place! My now 17-year-old has taken lessons with Tom since first grade.
        He's provided the right amount of support, encouragement, and challenge appropriate
        at each age and stage.&#8221;
      </p>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-full-text" hidden>
        &#8220;Love this place! My now 17-year-old has taken lessons with Tom since first grade.
        He's provided the right amount of support, encouragement, and challenge appropriate
        at each age and stage.<br><br>
        The studio itself is easy to reach, with free parking and a waiting area for parents.
        Plus its a short walk from shops and restaurants if you want to wander. My kid now
        walks from the HS for his lessons after school.<br><br>
        The recitals 2x/year are adorable and enjoyable. The older kids encourage the younger
        and everyone's efforts are celebrated. Each year, I'm particularly impressed by the
        adults brave enough to perform.<br><br>
        If you're looking for a music teacher who is right for you/your child, I encourage you
        to consider Red Barn. Their trial lesson policy is fair and useful.&#8221;
      </p>

      <button class="rbmgr-more-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">More</button>
    </article>

    <article class="rbmgr-card">
      <h3 class="rbmgr-reviewer">Johanna Neumann</h3>
      <div class="rbmgr-card-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-short-text">
        &#8220;Great teacher! Develops technique, and when you stick with it, it pays off &#8212;
        a lot, a lot, A LOT!&#8221;
      </p>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-full-text" hidden>
        &#8220;My child has taken guitar classes here since Fall 2021. When I asked him what he
        would write in a review he said: &#8216;Great teacher! Develops technique, which may not
        be fun when you're first learning it, but when you stick with it it pays off -
        a lot a lot A LOT!&#8217;&#8221;
      </p>

      <button class="rbmgr-more-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">More</button>
    </article>

    <article class="rbmgr-card">
      <h3 class="rbmgr-reviewer">Ben Schaeffer</h3>
      <div class="rbmgr-card-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-short-text">
        &#8220;Red Barn was friendly, welcoming, and accessible from the moment I arrived.
        It was a wonderful place to continue developing as a musician and performer.&#8221;
      </p>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-full-text" hidden>
        &#8220;I studied voice and piano at Red Barn Music School for about five years while
        attending Hampshire College as a Theater major. Red Barn was friendly, welcoming,
        and accessible from the moment I arrived. I had vocal training with Anne Kearns and
        studied piano with Tom Williams, who was a teacher I especially enjoyed working with.
        Having previously trained in New York and London, the Red Barn was recommended to me
        by my former vocal coach and piano teacher in New York. Red Barn proved to be a
        wonderful place to continue developing as a musician and performer. Thank you,
        Red Barn.&#8221;
      </p>

      <button class="rbmgr-more-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">More</button>
    </article>

    <article class="rbmgr-card">
      <h3 class="rbmgr-reviewer">Tania Linares</h3>
      <div class="rbmgr-card-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-short-text">
        &#8220;Kevin is a wonderful teacher &#8212; kind, encouraging, and incredibly patient.
        My son always looks forward to his next lesson.&#8221;
      </p>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-full-text" hidden>
        &#8220;Kevin is a wonderful teacher. My son is only four years old, and Kevin is always
        kind, encouraging, and incredibly patient with him. He knows how to make each lesson
        fun while helping my son feel comfortable and excited about learning music. My son
        loves Kevin and always looks forward to his next lesson. I wish there were more
        teachers like him!&#8221;
      </p>

      <button class="rbmgr-more-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">More</button>
    </article>

    <article class="rbmgr-card">
      <h3 class="rbmgr-reviewer">Troens Spring</h3>
      <div class="rbmgr-card-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-short-text">
        &#8220;An excellent group of teachers and a lovely school. The instructors genuinely
        care about their students.&#8221;
      </p>

      <p class="rbmgr-review-text rbmgr-full-text" hidden>
        &#8220;Red Barn Music School is an excellent group of teachers and a lovely school.
        The instructors genuinely care about their students. It is a wonderful school
        for anyone interested in learning music.&#8221;
      </p>

      <button class="rbmgr-more-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">More</button>
    </article>

  </section>

  <div class="rbmgr-buttons">
    <a class="rbmgr-button rbmgr-secondary"
       href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/3iUEfPBaUmL1Eftz8"
       target="_blank"
       rel="noopener">
      Write a Review
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="rbmgr-source-note">
    Selected excerpts from Google reviews. Use More to read the complete review text.
  </p>
</div>
</div>

<script>
document.querySelectorAll('.rbm-google-reviews-page .rbmgr-more-toggle').forEach(function(button) {
  button.addEventListener('click', function() {
    var card = button.closest('.rbmgr-card');
    var shortText = card.querySelector('.rbmgr-short-text');
    var fullText = card.querySelector('.rbmgr-full-text');
    var expanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';

    button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
    shortText.hidden = !expanded;
    fullText.hidden = expanded;
    button.textContent = expanded ? 'More' : 'Less';
  });
});
</script>
